          %p
            The observation that the would-be Poisson bracket induced by a higher degree closed form extends to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket+Lie+n-algebra"} Poisson bracket Lie n-algebra
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Rogers10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
                ,
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                  algebras from multisymplectic geometry
                , Letters in Mathematical Physics
                %strong 100
                1 (2012) 29-50 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1005.2230"}> arXiv:1005.2230
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://link.springer.com/article/10.1007%2Fs11005-011-0493-x"} journal
            %li#Rogers11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
                ,
                %em Higher symplectic geometry
                PhD thesis (2011) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.4068"}> arXiv:1106.4068
                )
          %p
            with first discussion of application to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantization"} prequantization
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
                ,
                %em 2-plectic geometry, Courant algebroids, and categorified prequantization
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.2975"} arXiv:1009.2975
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher geometric quantization
                %em Higher Structures 2011
                in Göttingen (
                %a{:href => "http://www.crcg.de/wiki/Higher_geometric_quantization"}> pdf slides
                )
          %p
            Discussion in the more general context of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+prequantum+field+theory"} extended prequantum field theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+geometric+prequantum+theory"} Higher geometric prequantum theory
                ,
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras+of+local+observables+from+higher+prequantum+bundles"} L-∞ algebras of local observables from higher prequantum bundles
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#deLeon12
              M. de León, S. Vilariño.
              %em Lagrangian submanifolds in k-symplectic settings
              (2012). (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1202.3964"}> arXiv:1202.3964
              ).
          %p
            See also the references at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+geometry"} multisymplectic geometry
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-symplectic+manifold"} n-symplectic manifold
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-generalization" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contact+geometry"} contact geometry
            in line with
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+geometry"} multisymplectic geometry
            = succeed "-plectic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              Luca Vitagliano,
              %em L-infinity Algebras From Multicontact Geometry
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.2751"}> arXiv.1311.2751
              )
          %h3#applications Applications
          %p
            Some more references on application, on top of those mentioned in the articles
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesGeneral"} above
          %p
            A survey of some (potential) applications of 2-plectic geometry in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            models is in section 2 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"}> Christian Saemann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
              %em Groupoid quantization of loop spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.5921"}> arXiv:1203.5921
              )
          %p and in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"}> Christian Saemann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
              %em Quantization of 2-Plectic Manifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.1890"}> arXiv:1106.1890
              )
          %h3#examples_2 Examples
          %p
            On
            = succeed "-plectic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxwell+theory"} Maxwell theory
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Maxwell+theory"} Einstein-Maxwell theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Petr+Ho%C5%99ava"}> Petr Hořava
                ,
                %em On a covariant Hamilton-Jacobi framework for the Einstein-Maxwell theory
                Classical and Quantum Gravity
                %strong 8
                11 (1991) 2069 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/0264-9381/8/11/016"}> doi:10.1088/0264-9381/8/11/016
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Vey"}> Dmitri Vey
                ,
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  \-Plectic Maxwell Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.2192"}> arxiv:1303.2192
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Vey"}> Dmitri Vey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Multisymplectic formulation of vielbein gravity. De Donder-Weyl formulation, Hamiltonian
                    = succeed "-forms" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
                %strong 32
                9 (2015) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.3546"}> arxiv:1404.3546
                ,
                = succeed "&lbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/0264-9381/32/9/095005"} doi:10.1088/0264-9381/32/9/095005
            %li
              %p
                Patrick Cabau, Fernand Pelletier.
                %em Partial Nambu-Poisson structures on a convenient manifold
                (2024). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.08688"}> arXiv:2404.08688
                ).
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/teleparallel+gravity"} teleparallel gravity
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+V.+Kanatchikov"}> Igor V. Kanatchikov
              \.
              %em The De Donder-Weyl Hamiltonian formulation of TEGR and its quantization
              (2023) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.10052"}> arXiv:2308.10052
              \&amp;rbrack;
